  "title": "Kourovka problem 20.99 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Conjecture: Let a1 G1 , . . . , ak Gk , k > 1, be finitely many pairwise disjoint left\ncosets in a group G with [G : Gi ] < ∞ for all i = 1, . . . , k. Then\n                 gcd([G : Gi ], [G : Gj ]) ⩾ k    for some 1 ⩽ i < j ⩽ k.\n   The conjecture is known to hold for k = 2, 3, 4.                               Z.-W. Sun",
